{#
	The zyppy_search form shell - the MODERN fragment template.

	IDENTIFIER, and why this file's placement is the exact OPPOSITE of the three
	legacy templates in this same bundle. Read this before moving anything.

	  * ZyppySearchController declares template: 'frontend_module/zyppy_search',
	    a name containing a slash. AbstractFragmentController::isLegacyTemplate()
	    is literally `!str_contains($templateName, '/')`, so the slash is what
	    selects the modern rendering path and the modern context shape (data,
	    headline.text, element_css_classes, ...) instead of the legacy one.
	  * For ContaoFilesystemLoader to register a bundle template under a
	    PREFIXED identifier, the directory has to be a namespace root - which
	    means an empty `.twig-root` marker file. Ours is at
	    contao/templates/twig/.twig-root. Without it, TemplateLocator scans
	    subdirectories at depth < 1 and registers this file as the bare
	    basename `zyppy_search`, the fragment's declared name never resolves,
	    and every render 500s.
	  * The three legacy templates - modules/mod_search_zyppy,
	    search/search_zyppy and search/search_zyppy_results - must KEEP their
	    no-marker placement. They are flat identifiers, and two of them are
	    reached through DCA dropdowns built by Controller::getTemplateGroup(),
	    which throws for any identifier containing a slash.

	Both are true at once because TemplateLocator::expandSubdirectories() walks
	the bundle's contao/templates tree, treats any directory carrying the marker
	as its own namespace root (scanned RECURSIVELY, giving prefixed names) and
	excludes that directory's children from the plain depth<1 scan the other
	subdirectories get. tests/Template/TemplateIdentifierTest.php pins both
	halves against the real core TemplateLocator rather than leaving it as prose.

	--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	CHANGED IN STEP 10: this shell renders RESULTS again.

	`results` is the first page, server-rendered by ResultRenderer through
	search_zyppy_results + search_zyppy. That is what gives the module a
	no-JavaScript fallback - a visitor who submits the form gets results back
	with no script involved at all - and it is the same string search.js later
	drops into div.results from the JSON route, so first paint and every live
	update are identical by construction.

	`mod_zyppy_search` on the wrapper is LOAD BEARING and is written out
	literally: element_css_classes carries only the editor's own cssID classes,
	not Contao's `mod_<type>`. public/js/search.js selects
	div.mod_zyppy_search, and contao-zyppy-popup's popup.js depends on it too.

	ESCAPED vs |raw. Twig autoescapes; the |raw values are `headline` (backend
	authored, may carry markup or insert tags) and `results` (already-rendered,
	already-escaped markup). Everything else is data and escapes - including
	`keyword`, which is attacker-supplied by definition, and `endpoint`, which
	is generated but still written into an attribute.
	--------------------------------------------------------------------------
#}
<!-- indexer::stop -->
<div class="mod_zyppy_search block{% if element_css_classes|default('') %} {{ element_css_classes }}{% endif %}"{% if element_html_id|default('') %} id="{{ element_html_id }}"{% endif %}>

	{% if headline.text|default('') %}
		<{{ headline.tag_name|default('h1') }}>{{ headline.text|raw }}</{{ headline.tag_name|default('h1') }}>
	{% endif %}

	<form{% if action|default('') %} action="{{ action }}"{% endif %} method="get">
		<div class="formbody">
			<div class="widget widget-text">
				<label for="ctrl_keywords_{{ uniqueId }}" class="invisible">{{ keywordLabel|default('') }}</label>
				<input type="search" name="keywords" id="ctrl_keywords_{{ uniqueId }}" class="text" value="{{ keyword|default('') }}" placeholder="{{ placeholder|default('') }}" data-min-length="{{ minLength|default(3) }}" data-error-text="{{ errorText|default('') }}" data-endpoint="{{ endpoint }}">
			</div>
			<div class="widget widget-submit">
				<button type="submit" id="ctrl_submit_{{ uniqueId }}" class="submit">{{ search|default('') }}</button>
			</div>
			{% if advanced|default(false) %}
				<div class="widget widget-radio">
					<fieldset class="radio_container">
						<legend class="invisible">{{ optionsLabel|default('') }}</legend>
						<span><input type="radio" name="query_type" id="matchAll_{{ uniqueId }}" class="radio" value="and"{% if queryType|default('') == 'and' %} checked="checked"{% endif %}> <label for="matchAll_{{ uniqueId }}">{{ matchAll|default('') }}</label></span>
						<span><input type="radio" name="query_type" id="matchAny_{{ uniqueId }}" class="radio" value="or"{% if queryType|default('') == 'or' %} checked="checked"{% endif %}> <label for="matchAny_{{ uniqueId }}">{{ matchAny|default('') }}</label></span>
					</fieldset>
				</div>
			{% endif %}
		</div>
	</form>

	<div class="results{{ popupClear|default(false) ? ' popup_clear' : '' }}">{{ results|default('')|raw }}</div>

</div>
<script src="{{ scriptSrc|default('') }}" defer></script>
<!-- indexer::continue -->
